# Configuring Access Control Lists (ACLs)

## Objective
Use Access Control Lists (ACLs) to control network traffic and restrict access between networks.

## Tools Used
- Cisco Packet Tracer
- Cisco Router
- Cisco Switch
- PCs

## Theory
Access Control Lists (ACLs) are used to filter network traffic and control which packets are allowed or denied in a network. ACLs improve network security by restricting unauthorized access.

## Network Example
Network A: 192.168.1.0/24  
Network B: 192.168.2.0/24  

Goal: Deny Network A from accessing Network B.

## Procedure

### Step 1: Enter Privileged Mode

Router> enable


### Step 2: Enter Global Configuration Mode

Router# configure terminal


### Step 3: Create Standard ACL

access-list 10 deny 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255
access-list 10 permit any


### Step 4: Apply ACL to Interface

interface fastEthernet0/0
ip access-group 10 in
exit


### Step 5: Verify ACL Configuration

show access-lists
show running-config


## Result
Access Control List was successfully configured to restrict network traffic.
